config ONTHE15_STATUS_INDICATOR
    bool "On the 15 two-LED status indicator"
    default n
    help
      Drive the P0.28 green and P0.29 red indicators from ZMK connection,
      battery, activity, and layer state.

config ONTHE15_STATUS_INDICATOR_SPLIT_SYNC
    bool "Send indicator settings from the split central to its peripherals"
    default y
    depends on ONTHE15_STATUS_INDICATOR && ZMK_SPLIT
    select ZMK_SPLIT_RELAY_EVENT
    help
      The ind_tog behavior is global, so toggling the connected indicator from
      a key reaches both halves on its own. A change made from Studio reaches
      only the central, which leaves the two indicators disagreeing. This
      relays the settings the same way the lighting module relays its own.

config ONTHE15_STATUS_INDICATOR_TEST_ALWAYS_ON
    bool "Hold both On the 15 status LEDs on for hardware tests"
    default n
    depends on ONTHE15_STATUS_INDICATOR
    help
      Ignore status patterns and continuously drive both indicator LEDs high.

config ONTHE15_LIGHTING
    bool "On the 15 lighting"
    default n
    select ZMK_MATRIX_LIGHTING
    select ONTHE15_LIGHTING_STARTUP
    help
      Turn on this keyboard's lighting: the reusable matrix lighting module
      plus the power-up intro. Enable ZMK_MATRIX_LIGHTING on its own for the
      module without the intro.

config ONTHE15_BT_FEEDBACK_BEHAVIOR
    bool "On the 15 Bluetooth feedback behavior"
    default y
    depends on !ZMK_SPLIT || ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL
    help
      Wrap Bluetooth profile selection and clearing so x15 status LEDs can
      provide deterministic feedback without relying on ambiguous BLE events.
